# Declared exemptions for the emitted-while check (emit-for-not-while).
#
# Format: file | fingerprint | reason
#   file        — basename of the koru_std source carrying the emitting site
#   fingerprint — the normalized `while (condition)` as the check extracts it,
#                 placeholders ({s}, {d}) included; stable across line churn
#   reason      — why the trip count genuinely is not nameable before the loop
#                 starts. Mandatory. An entry matching no site fails the check.
#
# An exemption is a ruling that this while is NOT a counted loop. Everything
# not listed here is a violation until converted to `for`.

io.blk.kz | while (_v > 0)                    | digit-extraction loop; the trip count is the digit count of a runtime value, unknowable before the divisions run (moved with the print.blk family split out of io.kz)
kernel.kz | while (i < nqf)                   | find-first search over queue families; breaks at the first compute-capable family
kernel.kz | while (m < mp.memoryTypeCount)    | find-first search over memory types; breaks at the first host-visible+coherent type
parser.kz | while (c.kids.len > 0)            | descent to the leaf of a parse tree; depth is a property of the parsed input
regex.scan.kz | while (__koru_pos <= {s}.len)     | scanner: the cursor advances by match length, one byte on an empty match, and breaks on no-match; trip count is match-dependent
regex.scan.kz | while (__koru_pos <= {s}.length)  | the |js variant of the same scanner — cursor advances by match length, breaks on no-match; trip count is match-dependent
pump.run.kz | while (true)                      | drain-until-quiescent event loop (zig and |js variants): it repeats the cascade until no live event remains; the trip count is however many rounds the writes generate — a data property, not a nameable bound
store.new.kz | while (__koru_cyc != -1)       | ancestor-chain walk by handles; chain length is data, not a nameable bound (covers all write-path emissions of the cycle guard)
store.new.kz | while (__koru_cyc !== -1)      | the |js emission of the same ancestor-chain walk
store.new.kz | while (__koru_sp > 0)          | explicit work-stack pop for preorder traversal; the stack grows while it drains
store.new.kz | while (__koru_i < __koru_store_{s}.len) | mutation-aware sweep: the store may shrink or grow mid-sweep, len is re-read every iteration and the cursor advances only when no removal occurred — the trip count does not exist before the loop runs
store.pverbs.kz | while (__koru_i < __koru_store_{s}.len) | same mutation-aware sweep emitted from the pverbs part file
store.query.kz | while (__koru_si < {s})      | the |js mutation-aware sweep: len is captured per iteration (__koru_len_before) because the store may shrink or grow mid-sweep
store.index.kz | while (__koru_ci.next())     | map-valueIterator drain on clear: the trip count is however many buckets the index holds — a data property, not a nameable bound
store.indexwalk.kz | while (true)             | removal-tolerant bucket walk (zig and |js variants): members move between buckets mid-iteration, so each pass re-reads the bucket and advances the cursor only when the member still sits at it — the trip count does not exist before the body runs
